  ($qb$ITEM-FIB-25PLUS-440$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The issue spans leadership boundaries, and the way responsibility is assigned will influence future accountability, trust, and organizational behaviour. The response should strengthen shared accountability without reducing a systemic issue to personal blame. A non-urgent message is sent outside another person's working hours. Complete the etiquette: 'I will not expect an immediate ______.'$qb$, $qb$response$qb$, $qb$reply$qb$, $qb$answer$qb$, $qb$reaction$qb$, $qb$apology$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$How can a team lead best ensure equal growth opportunities for quiet or junior team members during client engagements?$qb$, $qb$Implementing a structured presentation rotation framework supported by peer coaching and preparation sessions.$qb$, $qb$Requesting open volunteers for client meetings while encouraging quieter members to speak up.$qb$, $qb$Assigning major presentation slots directly to quiet members to force immediate public exposure.$qb$, $qb$Consulting with senior management before changing presentation responsibilities for key client accounts.$qb$, $qb$Reserving client-facing presentations for senior staff while assigning internal team updates to junior members.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Which behavior demonstrates a true accountability mindset when a newly deployed process update causes minor tracking errors?$qb$, $qb$Owning the mistake transparently with affected stakeholders, implementing an immediate fix, and documenting lessons learned.$qb$, $qb$Apologizing to affected teams and offering to process their daily reports manually until errors subside.$qb$, $qb$Explaining to stakeholders that initial system errors are standard when deploying complex operational updates.$qb$, $qb$Requesting an independent technical audit to determine whether the error originated from system tools or human input.$qb$, $qb$Focusing communications on the strategic long-term benefits of the new process update to maintain team morale.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the ethically sound action when discovering an entry error that artificially inflates team performance figures?$qb$, $qb$Rectifying the figures to reflect accurate data, documenting verified sources, and informing your lead of the correction.$qb$, $qb$Flagging the data variance to your manager and awaiting explicit instructions before making modifications.$qb$, $qb$Adjusting figures partially to match target goals while noting data collection adjustments in the appendix.$qb$, $qb$Leaving the reported figures unchanged for the current cycle while correcting collection scripts for future reports.$qb$, $qb$Submitting the report as compiled, assuming management evaluates annual rather than monthly productivity trends.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$How can a coordinator best foster workplace gratitude and resilience after an intense team project crunch?$qb$, $qb$Recognizing specific peer contributions publicly, facilitating a brief appreciation session, and ensuring rest recovery.$qb$, $qb$Sending a general thank-you email to the department highlighting upcoming quarterly performance goals.$qb$, $qb$Providing a catered team lunch while encouraging members to maintain high productivity for upcoming tasks.$qb$, $qb$Requesting that department heads acknowledge the team's hard work during the upcoming company newsletter.$qb$, $qb$Resuming standard daily routines immediately to help the team return to normal working hours without delay.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-042$qb$, $qb$A4-07$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What reaction demonstrates high feedback receptivity when a peer suggests communication format improvements?$qb$, $qb$Incorporating feedback gratefully, adopting structured formatting changes, and following up on progress.$qb$, $qb$Acknowledging peer comments politely while explaining why detailed background context was initially included.$qb$, $qb$Shortening future communications significantly by removing background details to keep messages brief.$qb$, $qb$Asking managers during routine check-ins whether they also find your communication updates overly detailed.$qb$, $qb$Accepting peer comments quietly while maintaining current writing habits for external communications.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-043$qb$, $qb$A4-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$How can an analyst effectively present complex operational data to non-technical business stakeholders?$qb$, $qb$Framing raw data metrics around a compelling problem-solution narrative that highlights strategic business impacts.$qb$, $qb$Displaying comprehensive financial data tables on presentation slides to ensure complete accuracy.$qb$, $qb$Focusing slides strictly on high-level general summaries, providing spreadsheets as optional add-ons.$qb$, $qb$Delivering a sequential numerical walkthrough, pausing after each data table to ask for questions.$qb$, $qb$Asking a technical colleague to present data tables while you handle introductory and closing remarks.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-REF-044$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is essential when handing off project updates to global collaborators working in different time zones?$qb$, $qb$Articulating clear context, tagging task owners, providing verified resource links, and flagging potential blockers.$qb$, $qb$Sending a brief summary message stating project progress and asking peers to check shared folders.$qb$, $qb$Scheduling late-night live sync calls to walk global peers through project updates verbally.$qb$, $qb$Uploading updated project files to shared folders, assuming peers will review revision histories independently.$qb$, $qb$Sending voice recordings detailing updates and asking peers to send messages if confusion occurs.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R1-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The same two people usually get the chance to present team work. What is the fairest improvement?$qb$, $qb$Rotate presentation opportunities with preparation support$qb$, $qb$Invite volunteers each time and encourage new people$qb$, $qb$Ask the usual presenters to choose their replacements$qb$, $qb$Give the next presentation to the quietest person$qb$, $qb$Keep the current approach because it already works$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
