  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R7-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate shares a template that makes your work much easier. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Thank them specifically and share how the template helped your work$qb$, $qb$Thank them and ask whether the template can be shared with others$qb$, $qb$Use the template and say thanks later$qb$, $qb$Share the template without mentioning who created it$qb$, $qb$Say nothing because templates are meant to be reused$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R7-044$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You finish your work late at night and a teammate will continue in the morning. What is the best handover?$qb$, $qb$Leave a concise update with status, open issue, next action, and links to the current files$qb$, $qb$State what is complete and what they should do next$qb$, $qb$Send the file links without an explanation$qb$, $qb$Send several messages describing everything you did$qb$, $qb$Wait until morning to explain it live$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R8-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A useful assignment is always given to people who have done it before, so newer colleagues never gain experience. What is the best improvement?$qb$, $qb$Give suitable newer colleagues a chance with clear support and fair selection criteria$qb$, $qb$Pair a newer colleague with an experienced person on the next assignment$qb$, $qb$Keep using experienced people because the task is important$qb$, $qb$Let experienced people choose who may join them$qb$, $qb$Wait until newer colleagues have more experience elsewhere$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R8-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You recommend an approach that later proves slower than a teammate's suggestion. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge the result, adopt the better approach, and share what you learned$qb$, $qb$Tell the teammate their approach worked better and use it next time$qb$, $qb$Explain why your approach seemed reasonable at the time$qb$, $qb$Keep your approach for some tasks to justify the earlier choice$qb$, $qb$Avoid discussing which approach worked better$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R8-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You find that a required check was skipped, although the final result appears correct. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Complete or arrange the required check and record the work accurately$qb$, $qb$Tell the owner the check was missed and ask them to complete it$qb$, $qb$Leave it because the final result looks correct$qb$, $qb$Mark the check complete because no error was found$qb$, $qb$Remove the check from the record$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R8-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague takes time to teach you a shortcut that is both safe and useful. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Thank them, apply it correctly, and acknowledge their help when sharing the improvement$qb$, $qb$Thank them and practice the shortcut on your next task$qb$, $qb$Use the shortcut and mention it only if someone asks$qb$, $qb$Present the shortcut as your own discovery$qb$, $qb$Ignore it because you already have a working method$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R8-044$qb$, $qb$A4-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague will review your request after you have logged off. Which message is best?$qb$, $qb$State the decision needed, key context, deadline, and where to find the supporting file$qb$, $qb$State the decision and deadline with the file link$qb$, $qb$Send the file and ask them to review it$qb$, $qb$Write 'urgent—please check'$qb$, $qb$Wait until you are both online$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R9-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member needs captions to follow an online training session. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Use an accessible session or enable accurate captions so they can participate fully$qb$, $qb$Enable available captions and check whether they work for the person$qb$, $qb$Send the recording afterward$qb$, $qb$Ask a teammate to summarize the training for them$qb$, $qb$Tell them to attend and read the slides$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R9-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You discover that a teammate's suggestion would fix a problem better than the solution you proposed. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Support the better solution and openly credit the teammate's contribution$qb$, $qb$Tell the teammate you agree and use their suggestion$qb$, $qb$Combine both solutions so your idea remains included$qb$, $qb$Ask a manager which solution should be used$qb$, $qb$Keep your own solution because you proposed it first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R9-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to copy a signature from an old document onto a new form to save time. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Refuse and obtain the required approval or signature through the proper process$qb$, $qb$Explain that the new form needs proper authorization$qb$, $qb$Copy it only if the same person would approve the form$qb$, $qb$Ask a coworker whether this is normally done$qb$, $qb$Copy it because the content is routine$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
