  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R1-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$How can a coordinator best foster workplace gratitude and resilience after an intense team project crunch?$qb$, $qb$Recognizing specific peer contributions publicly, facilitating a brief appreciation session, and ensuring rest recovery.$qb$, $qb$Sending a general thank-you email to the department highlighting upcoming quarterly performance goals.$qb$, $qb$Providing a catered team lunch while encouraging members to maintain high productivity for upcoming tasks.$qb$, $qb$Requesting that department heads acknowledge the team's hard work during the upcoming company newsletter.$qb$, $qb$Resuming standard daily routines immediately to help the team return to normal working hours without delay.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R2-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A development opportunity requires some prior exposure, but the same experienced employees keep receiving it. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Use transparent criteria and create supported entry opportunities so suitable less-experienced people can qualify$qb$, $qb$Publish the selection criteria and invite all eligible employees to apply$qb$, $qb$Continue selecting experienced people because they are lower risk$qb$, $qb$Rotate the opportunity regardless of readiness$qb$, $qb$Let managers nominate whoever they prefer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
