  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R8-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You discover that your mistake caused a small delay for another team. Other people have already acted on your earlier work. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Own the mistake, explain the fix, and prevent a repeat$qb$, $qb$Tell the affected team and correct the mistake quickly$qb$, $qb$Fix it quietly before anyone asks about the delay$qb$, $qb$Explain the circumstances that contributed to the mistake$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether the delay causes a real problem$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R8-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A report contains a figure that makes results look better, but you know the figure is wrong. The action may later be reviewed by someone outside the immediate team. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Correct the figure and record the accurate source$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager about the error before submitting$qb$, $qb$Add a note saying the figure may need checking$qb$, $qb$Leave it for this report and correct it next time$qb$, $qb$Submit it because the difference is small$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R8-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate stayed late to help you finish an urgent task. The response should reinforce the behaviour that helped the result. What is the most constructive response?$qb$, $qb$Thank them specifically for the help and its impact$qb$, $qb$Thank them privately before the next workday$qb$, $qb$Send a general thank-you message to the whole team$qb$, $qb$Assume they know their help was appreciated$qb$, $qb$Say nothing because helping teammates is expected$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team meeting is dominated by two confident speakers. The choice may shape who gets similar opportunities later. What can you do to improve participation?$qb$, $qb$Invite views from people who have not yet spoken$qb$, $qb$Ask everyone to give one short view before closing the topic$qb$, $qb$Let the discussion continue because anyone can speak$qb$, $qb$Ask the quietest person directly for an answer without warning$qb$, $qb$End the discussion once the confident speakers agree$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate finds an error in a file you prepared. Others have already acted on your earlier contribution. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Thank them, correct it, and check whether anything else was affected$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge the error and fix the file quickly$qb$, $qb$Explain why the error happened before making the correction$qb$, $qb$Ask them to correct it because they found it$qb$, $qb$Say the error is minor and does not need attention$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A coworker asks you to share a customer file they are not authorized to access. The action may be reviewed later by someone outside the immediate team. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Decline and direct them to the approved access process$qb$, $qb$Check why they need it before deciding what to do$qb$, $qb$Share only the parts you think are harmless$qb$, $qb$Send it if they promise not to forward it$qb$, $qb$Share it because they work in the same company$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R9-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A difficult week ends successfully because several teammates helped one another. The response should reinforce useful behavior for future work. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Recognize specific contributions and also note what the team learned$qb$, $qb$Thank the team and mention the successful result$qb$, $qb$Arrange a small celebration without discussing the work$qb$, $qb$Move straight to the next target while motivation is high$qb$, $qb$Focus only on the mistakes so the team improves$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R10-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A training opportunity has only two places and several suitable team members are interested. The selection may shape future access to similar opportunities. What is the fairest approach?$qb$, $qb$Use clear job-related criteria and explain how the places will be chosen$qb$, $qb$Compare who would benefit most from the training$qb$, $qb$Give the places to the people who asked first$qb$, $qb$Choose the most confident employees$qb$, $qb$Give both places to the most experienced employees$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R10-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your idea is praised in a meeting, but a teammate provided the key insight behind it. Others have already acted on the original idea. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Credit the teammate's contribution when accepting the praise$qb$, $qb$Thank the group and mention that others helped$qb$, $qb$Accept the praise and thank the teammate privately later$qb$, $qb$Say nothing because you presented the final idea$qb$, $qb$Let the teammate correct the record if it matters to them$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R10-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You notice that a coworker accidentally sent you confidential information you do not need. The information may later be reviewed outside the immediate team. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Do not use or forward it, and tell the sender so it can be handled correctly$qb$, $qb$Close the file and ask the sender what they want you to do$qb$, $qb$Keep the information but avoid discussing it$qb$, $qb$Delete your copy without telling anyone$qb$, $qb$Read it because it was sent to you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-2TO5-R10-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate helps solve a problem after your first approach fails. The response should reinforce the behavior that helped the outcome. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Recognize their help and use the lesson to improve the next attempt$qb$, $qb$Thank them and note what made their approach work$qb$, $qb$Thank them briefly and continue with the task$qb$, $qb$Focus on why your first approach failed$qb$, $qb$Avoid mentioning the help because the team owns the result$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
