  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R2-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You discover that a teammate's suggestion would fix a problem better than the solution you proposed. Senior stakeholders know you supported the original position, so changing course will be visible. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Support the better solution and openly credit the teammate's contribution$qb$, $qb$Tell the teammate you agree and use their suggestion$qb$, $qb$Combine both solutions so your idea remains included$qb$, $qb$Ask a manager which solution should be used$qb$, $qb$Keep your own solution because you proposed it first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R2-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to copy a signature from an old document onto a new form to save time. The information may influence a formal decision and must remain accurate under later scrutiny. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Refuse and obtain the required approval or signature through the proper process$qb$, $qb$Explain that the new form needs proper authorization$qb$, $qb$Copy it only if the same person would approve the form$qb$, $qb$Ask a coworker whether this is normally done$qb$, $qb$Copy it because the content is routine$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R2-010$qb$, $qb$A4-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A teammate notices a risk early and prevents rework for the whole group. The response should recognize contribution while also reinforcing behaviors that improve future collaboration. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Recognize the specific action and explain the rework it prevented$qb$, $qb$Thank them and tell the team what was avoided$qb$, $qb$Say 'well done' in the team chat$qb$, $qb$Move on because the problem never occurred$qb$, $qb$Focus on why the risk existed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R3-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A useful assignment is always given to people who have done it before, so newer colleagues never gain experience. The decision affects immediate delivery and the future development of less-experienced colleagues. What is the best improvement?$qb$, $qb$Give suitable newer colleagues a chance with clear support and fair selection criteria$qb$, $qb$Pair a newer colleague with an experienced person on the next assignment$qb$, $qb$Keep using experienced people because the task is important$qb$, $qb$Let experienced people choose who may join them$qb$, $qb$Wait until newer colleagues have more experience elsewhere$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R3-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You recommend an approach that later proves slower than a teammate's suggestion. Senior stakeholders know the history, so your response will signal how the team handles being wrong. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge the result, adopt the better approach, and share what you learned$qb$, $qb$Tell the teammate their approach worked better and use it next time$qb$, $qb$Explain why your approach seemed reasonable at the time$qb$, $qb$Keep your approach for some tasks to justify the earlier choice$qb$, $qb$Avoid discussing which approach worked better$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
