  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R5-007$qb$, $qb$A4-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The decision affects both immediate delivery and who gets the chance to build future capability. How can a team lead best ensure equal growth opportunities for quiet or junior team members during client engagements?$qb$, $qb$Implementing a structured presentation rotation framework supported by peer coaching and preparation sessions.$qb$, $qb$Requesting open volunteers for client meetings while encouraging quieter members to speak up.$qb$, $qb$Assigning major presentation slots directly to quiet members to force immediate public exposure.$qb$, $qb$Consulting with senior management before changing presentation responsibilities for key client accounts.$qb$, $qb$Reserving client-facing presentations for senior staff while assigning internal team updates to junior members.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R5-008$qb$, $qb$A4-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Senior stakeholders know the history, so your response will demonstrate how you handle being wrong. Which behavior demonstrates a true accountability mindset when a newly deployed process update causes minor tracking errors?$qb$, $qb$Owning the mistake transparently with affected stakeholders, implementing an immediate fix, and documenting lessons learned.$qb$, $qb$Apologizing to affected teams and offering to process their daily reports manually until errors subside.$qb$, $qb$Explaining to stakeholders that initial system errors are standard when deploying complex operational updates.$qb$, $qb$Requesting an independent technical audit to determine whether the error originated from system tools or human input.$qb$, $qb$Focusing communications on the strategic long-term benefits of the new process update to maintain team morale.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
