  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-17TO25-R10-009$qb$, $qb$A4-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A local adviser says a small unofficial payment is the only practical way to obtain a routine inspection on time. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Refuse the unofficial payment, document and escalate the issue appropriately, and pursue lawful alternatives even if timing is affected.$qb$, $qb$Take a reasonable immediate action on the visible issue and defer the broader structural question to the next formal review.$qb$, $qb$Gather additional evidence and make a limited adjustment without resolving the central trade-off.$qb$, $qb$Keep the current framework and ask affected leaders to manage its consequences.$qb$, $qb$Maintain the existing course until the risk becomes unavoidable.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
